```text
PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Public Services Committee was held on Monday, July 7, 2025, in Council
Chambers and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS:
Tom Segrave, Chairman; Dr. Michelle Aldrich; Dr. Kathy
Emmons; and Jeff White (via Zoom).
.
AGENDA ITEMS
II.
ORDINANCE —3”’ READING
— Annexing to the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, a portion
of land generally located east of South Greeley highway and north of Chalk Bluff Road.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 3rd and final reading, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Brandon Gilchrist, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and advised there
have been no changes to the proposed ordinance since approval on 2 reading. Brad Emmons,
AVI P.C., provided information related to the upcoming zone change to Business Park (BP).
Committee member Aldrich commented on the item.
12.
ORDINANCE _3rd READING
— Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne to assign a Zoning Classification of AG Agricultural to a parcel of land annexed
to the City, generally located east of South Grecley Ilighway and north of Chalk Bluff
Road.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 3”’ and final reading, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Brandon Gilchrist, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and advised there
have been no changes to the proposed ordinance since approval on 2’”’ reading.
Committee
member Aldrich commented on the item.
13.
ORDINANCE —3”’ READING
— Amending Section 10.04.050, Obedience Required, of
the Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, to clarify the default offense level
for violations of Title 10 of the Municipal Code.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 3 and final reading, seconded by Mr. White. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
John Brodie, City Attorney, provided a staff report and advised there have been no changes to the
proposed ordinance since approval on 2d1 reading.
```

### Page 2 of 3

```text
14.
ORDINANCE 31 READING
Amending Section 6.08.180, Feeding Geese and Ducks
Prohibited, of Chapter 6.08, Animal Care and Control Regulations Generally, of Title 6,
Animals, of the Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, to include seagulls
and extend the feeding prohibition to all property within city limits.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 3 and final reading, seconded by Mr. White. Dr. Aldrich moved
to amend 6.08.180(B) to read “Any person who violates this section shall be guilty of a
misdemeanor, punishable by a fine of not less than one hundred dollars ($100.00) and not more
than two hundred dollars ($200.00),” seconded by Mr. White,
Motion to amend failed by
unanimous voice vote. Dr. Aldrich moved to amend section 6.08.180(B) to read “Any person who
violates this section shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, punishable by a fine of not more than seven
hundred fifty dollars ($750.00),” seconded by Dr. Emmons.
Motion to amend carried by
unanimous voice vote. Main motion, as amended, carried by unanimous voice vote.
Dr. Aldrich, co-sponsor of the item, provided a staff report and advised there have been no changes
since approval on 2n’ reading.
John Brodie, City Attorney, and Captain David Janes, Police
Department, provided additional information. Committee members Aldrich, Emmons and White
commented on the item. Ward III City Councilman Mark Moody and Ward II City Councilman
Dr. Mark Rinne also commented on the item.
15.
ORDINANCE 2’” READING
— Amending and repealing multiple Sections of Chapter
9.24, Weapons, of Title 9, Public Peace and Welfare, of the Municipal Code of the City of
Cheyenne, Wyoming, relating to the sale, transport, discharge, possession and regulation
of firearms to better conform to state statute and avoid duplication with federal law,
(SPONSORS - DR. ALDRICh AND MR. MOODY)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 2 reading, seconded by Mr. White. Motion carried with Dr.
Aldrich and Mr. White voting “YES” and Dr. Emmons voting “NO.”
Ward III City Councilman Mark Moody, and co-sponsor of the ordinance amendment, provided
an overview of the proposed changes. John Brodie, City Attorney; David Ilopkinson, Deputy City
Attorney;
and Captain David Janes, Police Department, provided additional
information.
Committee members Aldrich, Emmons and White commented on the item. Mayor Patrick Collins
also commented on the item.
19.
RESOLUTION
— Directing that plans for the 15th Street Corridor Revitalization Project
preserve the Cheyenne Gunslingers’ current location, layout, buildings and landscaping at
West
15th Street and Pioneer Avenue. (SPONSORS
— DR. ALDRICII AND MR.
MOODY)
Dr. Aldrich moved to adopt. Motion died due to the lack of a second.
Ward III City Councilman Mark Moody, and co-sponsor, provided and overview of the proposed
resolution, Committee member Emmons commented on the item. Public comments were made
by Roger Barnes, Cheyenne Gunslingers, and Brian Bau.
```

